# Skald

Skald is the runtime layer in Wyrd. It owns provider clients, prompt execution,
tool resolution, agent loops, and workflow orchestration. Wyrd Cards describe
the components; Skald turns the runnable declarations into execution.

## What Skald owns

- Provider-specific request and response handling.
- Prompt construction and execution.
- Runtime tool registration and resolution.
- Bounded Agent loops and session state.
- Workflow composition and task execution.

Skald does not replace the Wyrd registry. A registered Prompt, Agent, or
Workflow Card remains the declarative source of truth; the runtime resolves that
contract when it executes.

